HST Sheets: no crash when the input line's delay timer fires before Calc ever used its edit engine.

ScInputHandler creates its EditEngine lazily (ImplCreateEditEngine, when a Calc view first edits
or activates through the handler). NotifyChange starts the 500 ms delay timer whenever the
active view is not a Calc view; DelayTimer then cleared the engine's text without checking that
the engine exists. When the first Calc document of a session appears while another window keeps
the focus (the start-up welcome or another modal dialog of the office, a document loaded from
another process), the timer fires with no engine and the office crashes: access violation in
EditEngine::SetUpdateLayout called from ScEditEngineDefaulter::SetTextCurrentDefaults, from
ScInputHandler::DelayTimer, from the scheduler inside the dialog's modal loop.

Measured on Windows 11 with the 1.0.1 release and 1.0.2 builds: a fresh profile, the Start
Center with the welcome dialog open, then Sheets loaded as the first document over UNO -> the
document recovery dialog of a crash every time; the office's fault note gave the frames
(mergedlo EditEngine::SetUpdateLayout+0x1f <- sclo ScEditEngineDefaulter::SetTextCurrentDefaults
<- sclo ScInputHandler::DelayTimer <- Scheduler::CallbackTaskScheduling <- Dialog::Execute <-
pyuno). With a Writer document opened first, or a Calc window that takes the focus, the handler
already has its engine and nothing happens.

With no engine there is no text to clear: the rest of the handler (input line reset) still runs.

--- a/sc/source/ui/app/inputhdl.cxx
+++ b/sc/source/ui/app/inputhdl.cxx
@@ -4642,7 +4642,10 @@
         bInOwnChange = true; // disable ModifyHdl (reset below)
 
         pActiveViewSh = nullptr;
-        mpEditEngine->SetTextCurrentDefaults( OUString() );
+        // HST Office: the edit engine is created lazily, when a Calc view first uses this handler;
+        // before that there is no text to clear (a first Calc document opened under a dialog)
+        if (mpEditEngine)
+            mpEditEngine->SetTextCurrentDefaults( OUString() );
         if ( pInputWin )
         {
             pInputWin->SetPosString( OUString() );
